pursuing advanced academic training in environmental science and management, geography, geology, or another related field.\nYou'll work closely with faculty who have expertise in a broad range of fields and often partner with government agencies and other science and environmental organizations in their research.\nAdmissions Requirements\nMeet PSU\u2019s minimum requirements\nExpected completion of a bachelor\u2019s or master\u2019s degree in a related field that will have prepared student to become engaged in state-of-the-art original research\nDeadlines\nThis program only admits students once a year for fall term: Jan. 15.\nApplication Materials\nBelow is the list of the information and materials you will need to provide as part of your application. We recommend preparing these materials in advance of submitting your application.\nStatement of Intent: Your statement should be about two pages long and discuss your motivation for pursuing a Ph.D. and your general area of interest. You should identify research groups and faculty members with whom you may be interested in working, as placement in the program is dependent upon available advisors.\nReferences: Submit contact information for at least three people who are qualified to assess your promise as a graduate student. Portland State University will contact your references and provide them with instructions for submitting recommendation forms.\nCopies of transcripts only from schools where a bachelor\u2019s degree was awarded and/or graduate-level coursework was completed.\nProof of English Language Proficiency (if applicable)\nStart Your Application\nabout this content\nContact\nIf you have any questions, please email the EES program director Andres Holz at holzc@pdx.edu.\nPortland State University\nSchool of Earth, Environment and Society\nPortland State University\n1825 SW Broadway\nPortland OR 97201\nPhone:\n(503) 725-3000\nEmail:\nsees@pdx.edu\nFacebook\nPSU X (formerly Twitter) profile\nInstagram\nYouTube\nB